# 高频词汇 List05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List05核心词汇

{{hypothesis}}{/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs/}{假设；假说}{The scientist tested the hypothesis through experiments.}}
{{identify}}{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ/}{识别；确认}{The study identified several risk factors for the disease.}}
{{illustrate}}{/ˈɪləstreɪt/}{说明；插图}{The case study illustrates the challenges of urban planning.}}
{{impact}}{/ˈɪmpækt/}{影响；冲击}{The policy had a lasting impact on the education system.}}
{{implement}}{/ˈɪmplɪment/}{实施；执行}{The school implemented a new anti-bullying policy.}}
{{implication}}{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn/}{含义；暗示}{The findings have important implications for public health.}}
{{imply}}{/ɪmˈplaɪ/}{暗示；意味着}{The data implies a strong connection between diet and disease.}}
{{impose}}{/ɪmˈpəʊz/}{施加；强加}{The government imposed new restrictions on travel.}}
{{improve}}{/ɪmˈpruːv/}{改善；提高}{The company is working to improve customer satisfaction.}}
{{include}}{/ɪnˈkluːd/}{包含；包括}{The package includes accommodation and meals.}}
{{increase}}{/ɪnˈkriːs/}{增加；增长}{The price of oil has increased significantly.}}
{{indicate}}{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/}{表明；指示}{The survey indicates a shift in consumer preferences.}}
{{individual}}{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl/}{个人的；个体}{Each individual has the right to freedom of expression.}}
{{inevitable}}{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl/}{不可避免的}{Change is an inevitable part of life.}}
{{influence}}{/ˈɪnfluəns/}{影响；势力}{Social media has a powerful influence on young people.}}
{{inform}}{/ɪnˈfɔːm/}{通知；告知}{The company will inform applicants of the decision by email.}}
{{initial}}{/ɪˈnɪʃl/}{最初的；开始的}{The initial findings were published in a leading journal.}}
{{innovate}}{/ˈɪnəveɪt/}{创新；革新}{Companies must innovate to stay competitive.}}
{{insight}}{/ˈɪnsaɪt/}{洞察力；见解}{The research provides valuable insights into human behavior.}}
{{instance}}{/ˈɪnstəns/}{实例；情况}{In this instance, the court ruled in favor of the plaintiff.}}
{{institute}}{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt/}{机构；设立}{The research institute focuses on renewable energy.}}
{{institution}}{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn/}{机构；制度}{Financial institutions play a key role in the economy.}}
{{integrate}}{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt/}{整合；融入}{The school works to integrate technology into the classroom.}}
{{intellectual}}{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl/}{智力的；知识分子}{Intellectual curiosity drives scientific discovery.}}
{{intend}}{/ɪnˈtend/}{打算；意图}{The company intends to launch the product next quarter.}}
{{interact}}{/ˌɪntərˈækt/}{互动；相互作用}{Children learn social skills by interacting with their peers.}}
{{interpret}}{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt/}{解释；翻译}{The law can be interpreted in different ways.}}
{{intervene}}{/ˌɪntəˈviːn/}{干预；介入}{The central bank intervened to stabilize the currency.}}
{{investigate}}{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/}{调查；研究}{The committee is investigating allegations of misconduct.}}
{{involve}}{/ɪnˈvɒlv/}{涉及；包含}{The project involves collaboration across multiple departments.}}
